/-!
# Finite free tensor reduction for a finitely generated field extension

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 045M (lemma-tensor-fields-CM), the finite free
map in the proof.
(blueprint: lem-trf-fg-field-tensor-finite-free-reduction).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

open scoped TensorProduct BigOperators

namespace Algebra

/-- A finitely generated field extension is finite over the subfield generated by a finite
transcendence basis. Tensoring this finite extension with any field extension gives the
specified algebra isomorphism and the specified finite free coordinate isomorphism.
The algebra structure in the conclusion is determined on pure tensors by the displayed
formula; it is the canonical map induced by the inclusion of the intermediate field.
No separability assumption is needed.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 045M (lemma-tensor-fields-CM), proof.
(blueprint: lem-trf-fg-field-tensor-finite-free-reduction).

Proof:
1. By lem-weil-pbc-finitely-generated-field-finite-transcendence-basis, choose a finite
transcendence basis t and put F = k(t). The original field generators also generate K over
F. Apply lem-weil-pbc-algebraic-generators-finite-extension to obtain a finite spanning
list, and discard dependent vectors to obtain a basis e. It has positive cardinality
because K is a nonzero vector space (def-weil-pbc-free-module).
2. By the tensor universal property (def-weil-pbc-module-tensor-product), the balanced
formula ((f tensor l) tensor z) maps to f*z tensor l. Its inverse sends z tensor l to
(1 tensor l) tensor z. Checking these formulas on pure tensors shows that the maps are
inverse and preserve multiplication, the unit, and the indicated A-algebra structure.
3. By lem-weil-pbc-free-module-base-change-free, the vectors 1 tensor e_i are a basis of
A tensor_F K. The preceding isomorphism sends them to e_i tensor 1, giving the displayed
coordinate isomorphism and finite freeness.
4. Apply lem-sc-affine-standard-cover-finite-free-local-fp-flat to deduce flatness,
interpreted by def-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map. The finite basis generates the algebra as a
module, so lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-is-integral gives integrality. -/
theorem exists_finiteFree_tensorProduct_reduction
    (k : Type u) (K : Type v) (L : Type w)
    [Field k] [Field K] [Field L] [Algebra k K] [Algebra k L]
    (hfg : (⊤ : IntermediateField k K).FG) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (t : Fin r → K), IsTranscendenceBasis k t ∧
      ∃ F : IntermediateField k K, F = IntermediateField.adjoin k (Set.range t) ∧
        ∃ d : ℕ, 1 ≤ d ∧ ∃ e : Module.Basis (Fin d) F K,
          ∃ (_ : Algebra (F ⊗[k] L) (K ⊗[k] L)),
            (∀ (f : F) (l : L),
              algebraMap (F ⊗[k] L) (K ⊗[k] L) (f ⊗ₜ[k] l) = (f : K) ⊗ₜ[k] l) ∧
            (∃ α : ((F ⊗[k] L) ⊗[F] K) ≃ₐ[F ⊗[k] L] (K ⊗[k] L),
              ∀ (f : F) (l : L) (z : K),
                α ((f ⊗ₜ[k] l) ⊗ₜ[F] z) = ((f : K) * z) ⊗ₜ[k] l) ∧
            (∃ β : (Fin d → F ⊗[k] L) ≃ₗ[F ⊗[k] L] (K ⊗[k] L),
              ∀ c : Fin d → F ⊗[k] L, β c = ∑ i, c i • (e i ⊗ₜ[k] (1 : L))) ∧
            Module.Free (F ⊗[k] L) (K ⊗[k] L) ∧
            Module.Finite (F ⊗[k] L) (K ⊗[k] L) ∧
            (algebraMap (F ⊗[k] L) (K ⊗[k] L)).Flat ∧
            (algebraMap (F ⊗[k] L) (K ⊗[k] L)).IsIntegral := by
  sorry

end Algebra
